--- A unit: a player, a monster, an object, a missile, an item. A handle: it names the unit by type
--- and id and is looked up on every use. It is not valid once the unit is gone, while its room is
--- unloaded (a monster comes back with its room, under the same id), and for a monster while it is
--- dead. Any member but `valid`, `id` and `type` then raises an error.
---@class Unit
---@field id integer The unit's id (its guid; ids are per type).
---@field type any 
---@field classId integer The row of its class table (MonStats for a monster, the class for a player).
---@field game Game 
---@field position Subtile 
---@field room Room? 
---@field level Level? 
---@field act any 
---@field mode integer The mode: what it is doing. Monsters and players narrow it.
---@field owner any? 
---@field distanceTo function Straight-line distance in subtiles.
---@field nearby function Units within radius subtiles of this one (itself excluded), optionally of one type.
---@field getStat function A stat's value with every modifier (life, mana and stamina in whole points).
---@field getBaseStat function A stat's base value, before modifiers.
---@field setStat function Set a stat's base value through the stat list; gold goes through the gold rules elsewhere.
---@field addStat function Add to a stat's base value.
---@field hasState function 
---@field addState function Put the unit in a state for frames (0: until removed). False when the engine refused.
---@field removeState function 

