--- A monster's body: the monster while it lies dead. A handle of its own, named by the monster's id:
--- valid while the monster is dead and its room loaded, and not valid once it is alive again (its
--- Monster handle is then valid) or gone.
---@class Corpse
---@field id integer The monster's id (its Monster handle has the same).
---@field classId any 
---@field baseId any The base class of its MonStats row (fallen1 for every Fallen).
---@field position Subtile 
---@field mode any 
---@field alignment any 
---@field targetable boolean Whether it can be selected and targeted (a corpse used up by a skill is not).
---@field champion boolean 
---@field unique boolean 
---@field leader Monster? The leader of the group it was in, when there is one.
---@field hasStateMask function 
---@field distanceTo function Straight-line distance in subtiles.

--- What a target scan found: the units it could attack within a squared distance of 1024 (about 32
--- subtiles). Distances are squared subtiles.
---@class TargetScan
---@field nearest any? 
---@field nearestDistance integer 
---@field weakest any? The one with the least life (whole points), the first of equals in the scan's order.
---@field weakestLife integer 
---@field nearestWhenPlayer any? The nearest, kept only when the scanning unit is a player: never for a monster (the engine tests the scanner).
---@field nearestWhenPlayerDistance integer 
---@field count integer 
---@field closeCount integer How many within a squared distance of 225 (15 subtiles).

--- A MonStats row as the AI reads it, for the game's difficulty. A snapshot: read it once.
---@class MonsterData
---@field id any 
---@field baseId any 
---@field ai any 
---@field aiDelay integer Frames between thinks when idle (aidel).
---@field aiParams table The AI parameters aip1..aip8 at [0]..[7]; what each means is the AI's (monai.txt).
---@field skills table Skill1..Skill8 at [0]..[7]; -1 for none.
---@field skillModes table Sk1mode..Sk8mode at [0]..[7]: the mode each skill is cast in.

--- What spawnMonster takes besides the monster and the place.
---@class SpawnOptions
---@field radius integer How far from the point to look for a free spot, in subtiles (default 4).
---@field minions boolean Spawn its minion group too (default false).

--- What the engine knows when a monster thinks. Updated before every think of the script.
---@class Think
---@field target any? The engine's pick of a target (AiTargeting.Advanced); with Default the script picks its own.
---@field distance integer The distance to the target as the engine measures it.
---@field engaged boolean Whether the monster is engaged in combat.

--- The monster AIs of a game, by MonsterAiId: every monster whose MonStats AI is the id.
---@class AiRegistry
---@field register function Run script as the AI. Targeting decides what think.target holds (default: none, the script picks).
---@field wrap function Wrap each think of the AI. Later mods wrap earlier ones; a wrapper that errors is removed.
---@field has function Whether a mod registered or wrapped the AI in this game.

--- The registries of a game: the declared ones and the monster AIs.
---@class GameRegistries
---@field ai AiRegistry 

--- One game, as one mod sees it. Everything registered through it is dropped when the game ends.
---@class Game
---@field id number The game's id in this process.
---@field tick number The current tick.
---@field storage function This mod's saved state for this game under key: the table saved there, or a copy of defaults
---@field loaded boolean Whether storage came from a save (or a reload) rather than starting empty.
---@field registry GameRegistries The behaviour registries of this game.
---@field difficulty any 
---@field expansion boolean 
---@field name string The game's name (empty in single player).
---@field seed integer The map seed.
---@field frame integer The engine's frame counter (25 frames a second).
---@field players function The players in the game.
---@field level function The level when it exists in this game now (never makes one).
---@field findUnit function A unit by type and id, when it is valid.
---@field unitsNear function Units within radius subtiles of a point, optionally of one type.
---@field spawnMonster function Spawn a monster at the free spot nearest a point or a unit, in an active room. Undefined when
---@field message function A system line to every player in the game.
---@field on function Subscribe to an event; undefined unsubscribes. One handler per event per mod.
---@field startScript function Start a script in this game, owned by this mod and, when given, by owner: it is dropped once
---@field waitEvent function Wait for an event of this game inside one of its scripts. The outcome is the payload.
---@field channel function Open a channel of this mod for this game.
---@field persist function The persisted state of owner in this game, created from a copy of defaults the first time;
---@field hasPersisted function Whether owner has persisted state in this game.

